{{SummarizeGuideBoxSets}}

==Phases==
===Overview===
We start the run by using {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}} to maximize some pet effects, as pets "keep going" during the skipped time. We do this with {{PetTooltip|Greater Chimaera}} to max sources (which only takes a few seconds) and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Pixie}} to generate a lot of autoclicks (usually 5-10min). We also cast {{SpellTooltip|Synthetic Entity}} for Void Entities during this time.

Then, we switch to {{PetTooltip|Mechanos Apexis}} and begin our main buildup. We stack {{SpellTooltip|Quasi-incantation}}, skipped time, and {{SpellTooltip|Ley Overdrive}}/{{SpellTooltip|True Sorcery}}. We also devote a portion of our time to {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Primal Elemental}} for its large Pet EXP bonus.

Then, we begin our burst: Void Mana, then snapping {{SpellTooltip|Stabilize The Flow}}, followed by {{SpellTooltip|Gem Resonance}}, and then finally swapping to our burst bar, where we can have 6 incantations because MA casts {{SpellTooltip|Kelphior's Black Beam}}.

===Step 1: Setting Up the Run===

{{GuideBox|pet=Greater Chimaera|pet1=pixie|
spells=#0#CharLVL@61,2;93,2;65,2;71,2;110,2;67,1|
items=#0#CharLVL@106;104;0;23;14;35;41;60;58;85;70;1008;210;300;410;405;90;2007;3007;504}}

'''Goals:''' 

* Max our sources with {{PetTooltip|Greater Chimaera}}
* Build up Void Entities and autoclicks for character EXP

Before we begin our main buildup, we want to build up some character experience, because Tempo scales its profits based on character exp (and also skips more time based on level). At the very start of the exile go to {{PetTooltip|Greater Chimaera}} to immediately max out your sources - it will take no time at all due to {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}}. After sources are maxed, swap to {{PetTooltip|Pixie}} to get autoclicks. 

This gear is not worth upgrading until EVERYTHING else is done.

Character experience from VE/clicks are logged, so you don't want to spend more than 5-10 minutes in this phase, or maybe 20 minutes for especially long exiles. Early on, this can result in ~1e9 VEs and ~1e14 ACs, whereas by the time you're approaching ascensions it might be more like 1e10 VEs and 1e15 ACs. Don't spend too long in this phase just to reach a certain number.

{{Note|If you still don't have enough character experience to reach Refined Wormhole near-immediately, then you may want to spend a small amount of time on {{ClassTooltip|class_name=Chronomancer}} with this gear set and a similar spell set (Singularity beam + SE + Wormhole, Pixie) to get some character experience to unlock Refined Wormhole. By the time you get to this guide, though, that should be unnecessary.}} 

