itemtab1=CPE Items|
items1=#2#CPE@101;115;6;24;12;32;41;68;56;85;77;1008;212;300;415;405;90;2007;3008;509}}

'''Goals:'''

* Cast {{SpellTooltip|Quasi-incantation}} as MUCH as possible, as it is our best source of time scaling. This thing is insane. Just trust me.
* Increase our skipped time with {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole|display_name=Wormhole}}, to scale our class ability
* Have {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Mechanos Apexis}} active, since it scales on real pet time
* Split up our buildup between different spells in our flex slot (see note on Cast Ratios below).

* {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole|display_name=Wormhole}} is log(Evo), so more Evo Eff doesn't help a ton.
* {{ItemTooltip|Temporal Scabbard|display_name=Spacepants}} and {{ItemTooltip|Eerie Turquoise Phylactery|display_name=Eerie}} should be enchanted to roughly 7-10 to keep up with QI/Wormhole costs. With spell memetics, you'll likely need more.

'''Gear Replacements:''' 
* {{ItemTooltip|Stabilizing Pauldrons}} and {{ItemTooltip|Timeshroud}}, are '''especially important to upgrade''', because they increase max Time Distortion, which directly increases your time skipped, and also massively increases profits from {{SpellTooltip|Stabilize The Flow}}. Prioritize them over any other gear in this set.{{ItemTooltip|Temporal Stabilizer}} is also equally, if not more, important, if you don't already have it maxed.
* If you don't have {{ItemTooltip|Charged Fin-Wing}}, use {{ItemTooltip|Empowered Water}}.
* If you don't have {{ItemTooltip|Ritual Disk}}, you can use {{ItemTooltip|Zenith, The Champion's Steed|display_name=Zenith}}. Disk is far better, though - prioritize completing the Brain Fog triumph if you plan to play Temporalist in the future.

Switch to {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Mechanos Apexis}}, and begin our main buildup. This will last for the vast majority of the exile. Temporalist enjoys longer exiles, because it has incredible time scaling, and MA's cast rate of KBB doesn't max out until 24h. However, you can still succeed with shorter runs; see what works for you. You lose nothing by bursting, besides the time spent not casting our buildup spells. For the majority of our exile, we use mostly the same spell and gear set as before, with some minor differences.

'''Cast Ratios''': In the second spell slot, we spend ~90% of the exile on {{SpellTooltip|Ley Overdrive}}, and the remaining 10% of the time on {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Primal Elemental}}. If you have low Evo Eff, meaning {{SpellTooltip|Primal Power}} increases your skipped time per wormhole by a significant (generally >30%) amount, then you should also spend some time on that. However, in this range, if you have full legendary gear, then that generally doesn't happen.

{{Note|Before spending too much time on buildup, do a quick burst (Steps 3-5) in order to get more upgrades (potentially more evocation efficiency, and more experience for MA).}} 
 

===Step 2.5: Offline Buildup===

{{GuideBox|pet=Mechanos Apexis|
spells=#8#OfflineScry@61,2;57,2;25,2;93,2;65,2;67,2|
items=#8#OfflineScry@115;101;6;24;14;32;41;68;56;88;77;1023;209;300;415;414;90;2007;3008;509}}

'''Goals:'''

* Maximize buildup while offline

'''This section of the guide was written before Wormhole applied offline (v1.58, June 2024). As of v1.77 (Oct 2025), Wormhole is, to my knowledge, still slightly bugged to not work fully while offline, but this may be fixed in the future. Right now, we still need to do this offline phase to make the most of it, but at some point in the future we will not have to.'''

This section of the guide only applies if you go OFFLINE (e.g. closing the game). Spell effects do not happen while offline, meaning that staying in our normal buildup set will only give us TS and QI casts. In order to squeeze a bit more out of our time while offline, we're going to scry our spells!

'''Gear Replacements/Notes:''' 

* If you don't have {{ItemTooltip|Ritual Disk}}, {{ItemTooltip|The Rubedo Engine|display_name=Rubedo}} is a replacement (although still significantly worse). {{ItemTooltip|Warp Basilisk}} can be a replacement of Rubedo, too, although it doesn't affect {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Primal Elemental|display_name=CPE}}.
* {{ItemTooltip|The Magnifier|display_name=Magnifier}} is here to multiply TS active casts by 2. Using {{ItemTooltip|Timeshroud}} could theoretically improve cast rates because of the increased max of time distortion, but in testing I didn't notice any difference, so go with Magnifier. 
* {{ItemTooltip|Stabilizing Pauldrons}} is in a similar vein to Timeshroud, except there's nothing else in the slot that matters. You should have these maxed anyways, but you can drop them for seemingly minimal effect.
* {{ItemTooltip|Temporal Scabbard|display_name=Spacepants}} is here to increase QI casts/s. Nothing else matters in their slot. 
* {{ItemTooltip|Eerie Turquoise Phylactery|display_name=Eerie}} can be used in place of {{ItemTooltip|Hectic Lime Phylactery|display_name=Lime}} if you can't sustain QI without it, but ideally you use Lime.
* {{ItemTooltip|Charged Fin-Wing}} is just here for the increased god EXP. If you don't have it, you can leave the slot empty.
* If a slot is empty, the items in it don't matter. Additionally, anything beyond this point can be ignored if you don't have it; they don't actively do anything to increase casts or benefit buildup.
* {{ItemTooltip|Light Of Eighth Star}} and {{ItemTooltip|Beholding Eye}} are just here for increased jar caps, because this is an offline set.
* Similarly, {{ItemTooltip|Spell Shards Fractalization}} is just here for shard gain because scrying can often be shard-intensive. This is especially helpful post-spell memes - you might even want to add in a couple other shard items in free slots, like {{ItemTooltip|Easymind Hat}}. These shard items are also the only reason is here.}}


It's not worth stacking {{SpellTooltip|Superposition}} very much, but we don't cast it anywhere else, so it may be worth swapping out {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Primal Elemental|display_name=CPE}} for some time (i.e. like 10 minutes total in a days-long exile. Seriously, not much).

This setup is simply '''maximizing''' offline profits. This is still '''significantly worse than being online''', and if you're playing Tempo, you should be trying to keep the game open as much as possible.

