===Step 5: Snap Phase===
'''Goals:'''

* Snap {{SpellTooltip|Stabilize The Flow}} and {{SpellTooltip|Gem Resonance}}.

Temporalist has 2 different spells it can snap: {{SpellTooltip|Stabilize The Flow|display_name=StF}} and {{SpellTooltip|Gem Resonance|display_name=GR}}. In this game, "snap" means that a spell will "snapshot" the incantation efficiency you had when you cast the spell, and retain that for its entire duration. You can utilize this by equipping as much incantation efficiency as possible, casting these spells, and then swapping to burst gear. StF and GR require slightly different sets to snap, because StF also snaps how much time distortion it consumes. We first snap StF, as it has a longer duration:

{{GuideBox|
pet=Mechanos Apexis|
spells=#4#TD-Charge@65,2;67,2;3,2;17,0;69,0;4,0|
itemtab=TD Charge|items=#4#TD-Charge@100;113;7;23;18;32;41;68;56;85;72;1005;209;301;411;409;91;2007;3001;509|
itemtab1=StF Snap|items1=#5#STF-Snap@100;113;7;23;18;32;41;68;56;85;72;1005;209;301;411;409;91;2007;3001;509|spells1=#5#StF-Snap@68,1;73,0;61,0;17,0;69,2;4,0|spells2=#6#Gem-Snap@68,1;57,2;61,2;17,2;69,0;4,2|items2=#6#Gem-Snap@100;113;7;23;18;32;40;68;56;84;72;1005;209;301;411;409;91;2007;3001;509|itemtab2=Gem Snap|t-spells=TD Charge|t-spells1=StF Snap|t-spells2=Gem Snap}}

These spell sets are the pre-burst setup, though this specific type of setup is also known as a [[Snap|"Snap"]]. Here's how it goes in this case: 
# Swap to TD Charge and wait for 30x TD. KBB is on the bar so that your weapon charges up, if necessary. 
# Swap to StF Snap. This will automatically cast Stabilize The Flow for you, with the snapped x30 TD value. Revert is active to ensure it doesn't run out, and other burst spells are added to charge them up with shards, if needed
# Swap to Gem Snap. This will automatically cast Gem Resonance with all of your incantation efficiency bonuses. Revert is active here for the same reason as above.
# Swap to Burst and enjoy the profits. If needed, you can swap back to the Gem Snap loadout to activate revert, which will refresh the duration of both Stabilize The Flow and Gem resonance.
'''Gear Replacements''':

* At enchant 34+5, {{ItemTooltip|Anointed Ashes}} is better than {{ItemTooltip|Heart of the Storm}}.
* {{ItemTooltip|Empowering Chestguard}} and {{ItemTooltip|Chronoboost Ring}} do not need enchants.

This seems complicated, but I promise it isn't actually that hard! You will have to get used to doing this, though.

